{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1471046-the-nova-underground-railroad","id":1471046,"title":"the Nova Underground Railroad?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-21T16:03:49-08:00","id":1471046,"title":"the Nova Underground Railroad?","content":"One thing struck me about the post-Ultimatum Era. <br /> <br /> There were friendly novas, both in Nippon and in the asteroid belt, working to help humanity.<br /> <br /> And the Aeon society knew about transcendence and the dangers of taint, but that equally, Novas' weren't <i>doomed</i> to go insane.<br /> <br /> But they sure probably would if they spent their life being hunted. <br /> <br /> So I had a thought of during the period between the end ofhte nova age, and the rise of the Psions, a secret agreement, deep and dark, where the Aeon Society helps find newly erupted novas, and, depending on their behavior and state, helps get them off world, while warning them about the dangers of Transcendence. Maybe a couple of Darkstar novas who had stayed even after Team tomorrow collapsed give them a hand.<br /> <br /> The risk of course is that &quot;The secretary will deny all knowledge of your actions if you are discovered&quot; because even the hint of working with Aberrants is a potential death sentence. So you'd have tgeams of Talents, maybe novas, maybe psiads, working to find newly erupted novas, evaluate them, and either deal with hem or help them get off world, all the while setting things up that to any outside observer, it was just a successful hunt of a dangerous aberrant.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T16:37:43-08:00","id":1471050,"title":"","content":"The whole thing that makes me dislike aeon society is after the nova era is project rewrite, I mean aeon society like to paint themselves as the good guys and helping humanity but they basically rewrite history to hide what happened and really at that point you know your in the wrong when you have lie and cover up stuff and demonize novas as the sole culprits who hold all responsibility for the aberrant war and that they are insane monsters and can't be anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T16:43:48-08:00","id":1471052,"title":"","content":"I really like the entire idea. It would be awesome to have a Agents of SHIELD stile campaign set after Ultimatum, where you are in the hunt of leftovers and when you find them you discover they are mostly hidden for being afraid and just trying to keep alive. At first the group don\u2019t know what to do with the few they judge non corrupted, but after some time the numbers are too big and they start questioning everything, grouping them to send them off planet.<br /> <br /> They start as Aberrant Hunters and become protectors of Novas, maybe even with contact to Warp capable novas to extract them, and some Nova Tech to be able to hunt the really crazy ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T17:29:11-08:00","id":1471057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1471046-the-nova-underground-railroad?p=1471052#post1471052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the entire idea. It would be awesome to have a Agents of SHIELD stile campaign set after Ultimatum, where you are in the hunt of leftovers and when you find them you discover they are mostly hidden for being afraid and just trying to keep alive. At first the group don\u2019t know what to do with the few they judge non corrupted, but after some time the numbers are too big and they start questioning everything, grouping them to send them off planet.<br /> <br /> They start as Aberrant Hunters and become protectors of Novas, maybe even with contact to Warp capable novas to extract them, and some Nova Tech to be able to hunt the really crazy ones.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It also makes me think of initial run of Marvel's X-Factor title back in the mid 80's when it worked under a false flag operation as a mutant-hunting service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T17:57:26-08:00","id":1471059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1471046-the-nova-underground-railroad?p=1471050#post1471050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole thing that makes me dislike aeon society is after the nova era is project rewrite, I mean aeon society like to paint themselves as the good guys and helping humanity but they basically rewrite history to hide what happened and really at that point you know your in the wrong when you have lie and cover up stuff and demonize novas as the sole culprits who hold all responsibility for the aberrant war and that they are insane monsters and can't be anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing is, that rewrite in the current setting appears to be less about &quot;and all novas are demons &quot; and more about &quot;Let's not let the various incomprehensible technologies that do bd things get lose.&quot; I mean, the whole changing the origin of various technologies might actually be necessary in order to simply have them adopted, rather than any sense of &quot;grrr, we're going to make novas look bad.&quot; <br /> <br /> I mean, to use an example, remember that the Glitch, from Distant worlds, destroy people's ability to use language, <i>even if they saw him at one remove</i>, via the opnet. So if you say: this new development it novatech, and we really don't understand it, but it's fine guys, promise, a lot of people are going to go: pull the other one. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, an interesting thing is, looking through the rules? A mostly mega-attribute nova, or one who isn't always pushing herself, can easily go her entire life without ever worrying about transcendence. So I could see more than a few novas just hiding after the ultimatum. They were late to the last boat, or didn't want to go, so now they're just hiding.*<br /> <br /> *I don't know if there are any rules on how the quantum flux on modern earth impacts transcendence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T18:14:45-08:00","id":1471062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1471046-the-nova-underground-railroad?p=1471057#post1471057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also makes me think of initial run of Marvel's X-Factor title back in the mid 80's when it worked under a false flag operation as a mutant-hunting service.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like the idea, I hate the example. The original X-Factor was a scheme cooked up by mutant hater Cameron Hodge, and involved tricking the original X-Men into making a Ghostbusters style commercial where they promised to show up and permanently eliminate American citizens if you called them. No TV network balked at running those commercials, no law enforcement agency interceded to stop them from kidnapping/killing members of a minority group, and no social activist protested the actions of supposedly murderous mercenaries acting on US soil.<br /> <br /> This is also the same era when Hodge's The Right organization stuck a pair of guys in flying armored suits and had them fly around New York City shouting about how they were murderous mutants out to destroy humanity, and not only did the news reporters believe them, they also had no clue what &quot;mutants&quot; were, despite the Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver being prominent members of the Avengers and living only a few blocks away in Avengers mansion. The Marvel Universe is truly a dystopian hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}